## What each owned module/method does
### Original import groundwork, September 25
- `logic/ImportFileValidator.java`: `validate(Path)` verifies presence, regular file, readability, and .txt extension before a worker begins. It returns a user-facing message instead of exposing filesystem exceptions.
- `logic/ImportSummary.java`: immutable file-local counts and timing returned to the UI. `distinctWordCount` was integrated October 16.
- `logic/TextFileAnalyzer.java`: `analyze(Path, cancelled, progress)` preserves a standalone API; `analyze(Path, Vocabulary, cancelled, progress)` uses a supplied (typically staged) vocabulary; `countLines` enables determinate progress; `checkCancelled` allows early termination.

### File-import JavaFX workflow, October 9–30
- `ui/TextImportTask.java`: the constructor receives file/path and shared controller, and `call()` runs the import outside JavaFX while updating Task message and progress properties.
- `ui/ImportController.java`: `setApplicationController` injects logic; `setOnImportCompleted` registers a UI-only callback; `initialize` establishes listeners and disabled states; `onBrowseFile` opens a .txt chooser; `onAnalyzeFile` creates and observes a single-use worker; `onCancelAnalysis` requests cancellation.
- `getValidatedPath` and `refreshValidation` check input and provide immediate feedback; `setBusy` disables inappropriate controls; `finishTask` unbinds worker properties; `formatSummary` and `formatFailure` give readable UI messages.
- `import-view.fxml`: input path, browse/analyze/cancel controls, progress, status, and read-only import summary.
- Shared integration: `ApplicationController.importFile` stages then merges learned data only after success; `Vocabulary.mergeFrom` combines complete word/follower totals; `Word.addCounts` combines staged counters; startup tab callbacks refresh/gate Generate and Autocomplete without cross-controller coupling; `GenerateController.setGenerationControlsDisabled` prevents invalid actions before any learned words exist.

### Autocomplete JavaFX workflow, October 30–November 6
- `ui/AutocompleteController.java`: `setApplicationController` injects shared logic; `initialize` observes typing and selection; `refresh` updates vocabulary-dependent state; `onUseSuggestion` inserts and records a selected follower without replaying text events.
- `onTextChanged` recognizes only completed words, avoids triggering on deletion/rewrites, and records known followers or confirmed unfamiliar words; `confirmAddUnknownWord` asks Yes/No before any unknown word is learned, treating dismissal as No.
- `showSuggestionsForLastCompletedWord`/ `showSuggestions` request and display ranked followers; `completedWords` normalizes text; `endsWithCompletionDelimiter` recognizes space/period/comma; `clearSuggestions` removes stale choices; `setControlsDisabled` gates the editor before vocabulary exists.
- Minimal supporting methods in existing team logic: `ApplicationController.isKnownWord` reads recognition status; `ApplicationController.addUserWord` persists a confirmed standalone word; `Vocabulary.addUserWord` adds the word without creating a fake follower relationship.
- `autocomplete-view.fxml`: sentence input, next-word suggestions, selection button, and status messages.

### Tests and verification
- `ApplicationControllerImportIntegrationTest` (October 30): successful file import feeding generation; cancellation after staged lines leaves no partial vocabulary.
- `AutocompleteIntegrationTest` (October 30, updated November 6): follower ordering, new choice recording, check-recognition and add-standalone-word API. The UI dialog itself still needs manual JavaFX testing.
- Manual acceptance check for November 6: import "the cat" and "the dog", type "the " to see suggestions; type "the turtle " and choose No to leave turtle unknown; type a different unknown word and choose Yes to add it; type an unknown first word and choose Yes to confirm it can be saved without a fake prior word.
